			<div class="content" id="post-content-4012956">
									

<p>Don't think you know good poetry when you see it, Nathan. Because this is some goddamn good poetry. My 13th-grade English teacher would tell me that, and she was picky and cynical to no end.</p>
<p>It's not a meme, it's an actual art form.<br />
One that is beautiful and causes readers to really think about the work and its nature.</p>
<p><sub>Also, roses are red, violets are blue is very cliche poetry base and only works under certain conditions.</sub></p>

							</div>

								
					
